            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0678" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.512/2307: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-18T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1921. Your despatch 1842, February 25.</p>
                <p>Referring generally to objections previously urged by this Government against
                    Mexican petroleum decrees, protest against attempt apparently contemplated by
                    circular February 18 [<hi rendition="#italic">19</hi>] to collect royalties from
                    American petroleum interests.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
